    "referenceAnswerEn": "(a) The data are already arranged in ascending order and there are 8 values.\nMedian $= \\dfrac{64 + 64}{2} = 64$.\nMean $= \\dfrac{52 + 58 + 61 + 64 + 64 + 70 + 73 + 90}{8} = \\dfrac{532}{8} = 66.5$.\n(b) The corrected data are $52,\\ 58,\\ 61,\\ 64,\\ 64,\\ 68,\\ 70,\\ 73$.\nThe median is still $\\dfrac{64 + 64}{2} = 64$ and is unchanged.\nMean $= \\dfrac{510}{8} = 63.75$, a decrease of 2.75.\nReason: the median depends only on the value at the central position of the ordered data. Changing the largest value from 90 to 68 still leaves it after the two central values, so those two values, and therefore the median, are unchanged. The mean is determined jointly by every value, so a change in any one of them alters the total directly, which is why the mean is sensitive to extreme values.",
